 "reading": "Accuracy: the closed reader is not more accurate than the free prompt with null allowed on any of the three sets (no paired difference is significant; on P1 and P6 the free prompt is ahead in point estimate). What the closed design buys: every value it returns is a date printed in the document, with page and span from the lattice, by construction; the free prompt's values are printed in the document almost always too, but a checkable quote comes with only about half of them, and a printed-date filter added after a free prompt would give the no-invention guarantee as well. The margin orders the closed reader's values for review; the free prompt has only its quote flag."
